-- Package names, binaries, identifiers and UI strings are still upstream's.
+## Changed in stage 2 (gate wired and tested)
+
+- Default config exposes one model endpoint: the OpenVault custom endpoint at
+  `${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/v1` (librechat.example.yaml). Every direct provider
+  block and example was removed.
+- `.env.example` sets `ENDPOINTS=custom,agents` and `NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL`; every
+  model-provider key field (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Azure, Bedrock, Assistants
+  and the "known endpoints" list) was removed. AirGPT holds no provider key.
+- Memory (cross-chat and user memory) is `disabled: true`, `personalize: false`
+  by default, labeled ungoverned in the config, in the Memories panel and in the
+  agent memory capability text, until it routes through Cortex actions.
+- App title fallbacks, the HTML title, the About diagnostics line and five English
+  UI strings say AirGPT. Root package name, container names and the default
+  MongoDB database name say AirGPT.
+- Gate test: `packages/data-provider/specs/airgpt-gate.spec.ts` parses the two
+  default config files with the real schema and fails on the upstream defaults.
+
+## Not done yet (stage 3)
+
+- Scoped package names (`@librechat/*`, `librechat-data-provider`), the
+  `librechat.yaml` file name, the `LIBRECHAT_*` env names and upstream container
+  image names are unchanged: each needs a build and a rebase plan to rename.
+- Tool keys for search, image generation and speech are still fields in
+  `.env.example` (blank or commented). They are not model endpoints, and the
+  Netie answer (route them through Cortex tool_runner) is not wired.
+- Retrieval does not yet call `netie.airgpt retrieve_space`; upstream RAG is
+  untouched.
 - SECURITY, SUPPORT and CONTRIBUTING contacts and URLs still point at upstream.
-- Translated docs, changelogs and third-party notices are untouched.
-- Netie gate wiring: Endpoints -> OpenVault /v1 only. Retrieval -> netie.airgpt retrieve_space. Cross-chat memory abstains until governed.
+- Translated UI strings, changelogs, helm charts and third-party notices are
+  untouched.
+- Whether OpenVault `/v1` needs a seat token and whether it serves `/v1/models`
+  is not measured here; `fetch: false` and the literal `apiKey: 'openvault'`
+  are the honest defaults until it is.
